│ Phase 1 — Correctness fixes that gate everything else                              │
│                                                                                    │
│ These change what the numbers mean, so they land before any tuning.                │
│                                                                                    │
│ 1a. Cross-stream allocator hazard in the activation double buffer                  │
│                                                                                    │
│ File: sae_trainer_rolling.py, _ActivationDoubleBuffer.next_batch (~1866)           │
│                                                                                    │
│ The batch is allocated on self._transfer_stream and consumed on the default        │
│ stream. There is no record_stream call anywhere in the repo (verified by           │
│ grep). When the training loop drops its reference, the allocator may return that   │
│ block to the transfer stream's pool while the default stream still has queued      │
│ kernels reading it. That is silent activation corruption, and it would present as  │
│ unexplained run-to-run quality variance rather than a crash.                       │
│                                                                                    │
│ Fix: call gpu.record_stream(torch.cuda.current_stream()) before returning.         │
│ One line. Highest severity-to-effort ratio in the plan.                            │
│                                                                                    │
│ 1b. Early-stop EV is computed on the training batch                                │
│                                                                                    │
│ File: sae_trainer_rolling.py, ~2827-2839; consumed at ~2899                        │
│                                                                                    │
│ total_var comes from full_batch and recon_val is the loss from the step just       │
│ optimized on that same batch. ev_perdim probes acts_mb, also training data.        │
│ This EV reaches scheduler.step and drives pin_ev_count, which gates                │
│ termination through pin_ev_patience — so an optimistically biased EV stops runs    │
│ early on flattering numbers.                                                       │
│                                                                                    │
│ Fix: hold out a fixed slice of activations the optimizer never consumes; compute   │
│ the control EV there. Keep the training-batch EV for logging under a distinct      │
│ name. Assert held-out indices never enter a training microbatch.                   │
│                                                                                    │
│ (Note: the ultra review cited line 3260 for this. That is a config block. The      │
│ real site is 2830-2831.)                                                           │
│                                                                                    │
